Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(migrate):=20Beads=E2=86=92Kernel=20transfe?=
 =?UTF-8?q?r=20is=20explicit-only,=20drop=20implicit=20auto-migrate=20(a7e?=
 =?UTF-8?q?1443c)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`forge migrate` is now the SOLE Beads→Kernel invocation path. It is only ever
run explicitly; NO default path may trigger a migration. Removed every implicit
auto-migrate call site and the machinery that served them:

- lib/commands/_resolve-command-opts.js: deleted runRuntimeAutoMigrate + both
  call sites (fired on EVERY kernel command — the highest-impact one).
- lib/commands/init.js: `forge init` no longer auto-migrates; it only installs
  git hooks.
- lib/commands/setup.js: deleted autoMigrateBeadsToKernel + its two call sites +
  export, and dropped the now-dead autoMigrateBeads no-op in defaultRunInit.
  `promptBeadsSetup` stays — it only provisions the Kernel issue store (banner +
  ensureKernelIssueStore), it never migrated Beads, so it is not a migration path.
- lib/commands/migrate.js: deleted the now-orphaned exports the call sites used —
  autoMigrateBeadsAtRuntime, autoMigrateBeadsIfPresent, detectBeadsJsonlSource,
  the in-DB import-marker ledger helpers, and the nudge string. The command
  surface (runBeadsMigration + honest gap report) is untouched.

Net effect: setup/init/every-command never auto-migrate or prompt for Beads.
The one-time "issues appear to vanish on upgrade" safety net is intentionally
gone per the retirement charter — users run `forge migrate --from beads` when
they want the transfer.

TDD: renamed the two behavior tests to pin the inverse contract —
runtime-no-auto-migrate.test.js (a kernel command in a repo with a live .beads/
store imports NOTHING; the hooks are undefined on every module) and
setup-no-auto-migrate.test.js (setup exposes no seam; explicit
`forge migrate --from beads` still works offline). Flipped the init-onboarding
test to assert init never auto-migrates. Full affected suite: 91 pass / 0 fail;
eslint clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
